{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1650","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Deletions of Two Adjacent Letters"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The string $$$s$$$ is given, the string length is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"odd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" number. The string consists of lowercase letters of the Latin alphabet."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As long as the string length is greater than $$$1$$$, the following operation can be performed on it: select any two adjacent letters in the string $$$s$$$ and delete them from the string. For example, from the string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"lemma"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" in one operation, you can get any of the four strings: \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"mma"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"lma"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"lea"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"lem"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" In particular, in one operation, the length of the string reduces by $$$2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Formally, let the string $$$s$$$ have the form $$$s=s_1s_2 \\dots s_n$$$ ($$$n \\gt 1$$$). During one operation, you choose an arbitrary index $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\lt n$$$) and replace $$$s=s_1s_2 \\dots s_{i-1}s_{i+2} \\dots s_n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the given string $$$s$$$ and the letter $$$c$$$, determine whether it is possible to make such a sequence of operations that in the end the equality $$$s=c$$$ will be true? In other words, is there such a sequence of operations that the process will end with a string of length $$$1$$$, which consists of the letter $$$c$$$?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input data contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^3$$$) — the number of input test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The descriptions of the $$$t$$$ cases follow. Each test case is represented by two lines:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" string $$$s$$$, which has an odd length from $$$1$$$ to $$$49$$$ inclusive and consists of lowercase letters of the Latin alphabet; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" is a string containing one letter $$$c$$$, where $$$c$$$ is a lowercase letter of the Latin alphabet. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case in a separate line output:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if the string $$$s$$$ can be converted so that $$$s=c$$$ is true; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" otherwise. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in any case (for example, the strings "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" will be recognized as a positive response)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\nabcde\nc\nabcde\nb\nx\ny\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\na\ncontest\nt\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nNO\nNO\nYES\nYES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, $$$s$$$=\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"abcde"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". You need to get $$$s$$$=\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". For the first operation, delete the first two letters, we get $$$s$$$=\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cde"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". In the second operation, we delete the last two letters, s